# Secrets doctrine (workspace non-negotiable #1): the ENV FILE ITSELF is the
# thing that never enters git. Values live in Bao (lumen/{env}); env.yaml
# (the LOADABLE dev template copy — `make config-init`) is a VALUE carrier
# the moment a dev fills it in, so it is ignored by its plain name.
# env.yaml.sample stays tracked (negated below) — it is valueless by design.
.env
.env.*
env.yaml
!.env.example
!env.yaml.sample
*.local

# build artifacts — ROOT-ANCHORED (/lumen) on purpose: bare names match at
# ANY depth and silently ate cmd/lumen & cmd/seed for the whole milestone
# (branch audit caught it; a clone of the branch would not have compiled)
/bin/
/dist/
/lumen
/seed
# dev-plane AppRole exports (make dev-plane output — throwaway values but
# still: generated env files stay out of git, doctrine §1)
/dev-plane.env

# local data
pgdata/
*.db
.vite/
